{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/837971-rule-question-firearms","id":837971,"title":"Rule question (firearms)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-27T00:39:57-08:00","id":837971,"title":"Rule question (firearms)","content":"Hi guys, <br /> <br /> I need some clarification about something firearms.<br /> The rule geek and l in my rounds have a heated discussion (English is not our native language) if additional successes carry on as extra dice for damage to roll, when attacking with firearms. <br /> He says no, I say yes. For me it's clearly stated in the general rule that all success after the first will be additional damage dice. <br /> His derivated his point of view from the Automatic fire maneuver, which stated that all extra successes do more damage so you only get extra damage after using maneuvers. I myself think that it's been written in the maneuver to clarify that this is a single attack. <br /> <br /> Sorry for such an easy question but I hope you can help to sort out this mess. Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T01:26:13-08:00","id":837976,"title":"","content":"Extra successes from the initial attack, regardless of whether or not you're using a maneuver, add additional dice of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T02:26:29-08:00","id":837985,"title":"","content":"Ben Quo is correct, though that is something that is a bit edition dependent. Earlier editions of the game didn't have it be a universal thing, but by Revised and the 20th books, it has been phrased as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}